plugin-db-qualification (2026110901) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The x86-64 fedora44 class, one set per cell, provisional tier: ten sets
    of 1109 records of 668 plugins, at 48000/64, 48000/128, 48000/256,
    48000/512, 96000/64, 96000/128, 96000/256, 96000/512, 192000/256 and
    192000/512, measured by plugin-qualify-sync on JACK's dummy driver
    without real-time priority, host profile omx-clap-host. Eight sets ran
    plugin-qualify 0.19.1, plugin-hostd 0.19.1 and omx-clap-host 0.30.6;
    48000/128 and 48000/256 ran 0.20.0, 0.20.0 and 0.31.0. Each set's
    provenance names its packages. 192000/128 is not here: its run did not
    finish. The crash, hang and unmeasured verdicts hold; the cost, latency
    and xrun figures are not reference figures. Built as RPMs.
  * The rpi5 zynthian-vangelis set is labelled the hardware tier: measured
    on the device's own audio interface.
  * Every records package requires plugin-qualify 0.20.1 up to 0.21, which
    takes a set by its cell, and provides plugin-qualification-records.

